  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Orange Corners: K2K in Burundi</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The purpose of this project is to inspire, support and build the capacity of knowledge institutes in Burundi, to provide more entrepreneurial forms of education. The project will support universities to make two or three courses of their choice more entrepreneurial. The universities may choose courses on entrepreneurship, but also other courses that should become more practical. Additionally, a design challenge will be organised as a grand finale of the project.The design challenge will be a competition between student teams from the various participating universities. A business will provide the students with an actual challenge within this business to which the students should design a solution. This will provide an example of how a practical student competition around local challenges can stimulate and facilitate fruitful collaboration between the private sector and knowledge institutes, and show the value of more practical and entrepreneurial forms of education.The active involvement of lectors in organising the design challenge and supporting the student teams will serve as capacity strengthening and empower them to integrate entrepreneurial forms of teaching in their current curricula.</narrative>
  </description>
